---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="CLI reference"
  description="OpsRun commands: validate, plan, run, resume, audit, hosts, and version."
  path="/docs/cli"
>
  <p>
    Entry point: <code>opsrun</code>. Global help: <code>opsrun --help</code>. Every
    subcommand also accepts <code>--help</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="validate">opsrun validate</h2>
  <pre><code>opsrun validate &lt;runbook.md&gt;</code></pre>
  <p>
    Parse the Markdown AST, build the domain model, run the validator. Prints findings
    with step id and source position. Exit non-zero on errors.
  </p>

  <h2 id="plan">opsrun plan</h2>
  <pre><code>opsrun plan &lt;runbook.md&gt; [--config PATH] [--var k=v] [--vars-file PATH]</code></pre>
  <p>
    Show execution order, dependencies, targets, and strategy. No remote execution.
  </p>

  <h2 id="run">opsrun run</h2>
  <pre><code>opsrun run &lt;runbook.md&gt; \
  --config opsrun.yaml \
  [--interactive] \
  [--dry-run] \
  [--strategy all|rolling|canary] \
  [--batch-size N] \
  [--max-failure-percent N] \
  [--var k=v] \
  [--vars-file PATH] \
  [--output text|json]</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li><code>--interactive</code> — approval prompts / TUI on a real terminal</li>
    <li><code>--dry-run</code> — preview without applying host changes</li>
    <li><code>--strategy rolling|canary</code> — gradual host rollout</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="resume">opsrun resume</h2>
  <pre><code>opsrun resume &lt;run-id&gt; --checkpoint-dir .opsrun/checkpoints</code></pre>
  <p>
    Continue an interrupted or partially failed run from the last checkpoint. The run
    id is printed at the end of a run (and recorded in the audit log).
  </p>

  <h2 id="audit">opsrun audit</h2>
  <pre><code>opsrun audit verify --log ./audit/opsrun-audit.jsonl
opsrun audit export --log ./audit/opsrun-audit.jsonl --run-id &lt;run-id&gt;</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>verify</code> checks the hash chain (and signatures when configured).
    <code>export</code> renders a post-mortem timeline for one run.
  </p>

  <h2 id="hosts">opsrun hosts</h2>
  <pre><code>opsrun hosts list --config opsrun.yaml</code></pre>
  <p>Inspect inventory hosts and groups from the active config.</p>

  <h2 id="version">opsrun version</h2>
  <pre><code>opsrun version</code></pre>

  <h2 id="config-precedence">Config precedence</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Command-line flags</li>
    <li>Environment variables (<code>OPSRUN_*</code>)</li>
    <li>Config file (<code>--config</code> / <code>OPSRUN_CONFIG</code>)</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Details: <a href="/docs/configuration">Configuration</a>.</p>
</DocsLayout>
